    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Turn**: Draw one (stock or discard top), discard one. Hand stays at 5 cards until a call. 2. **Call**: With a winning combination after drawing, place it face up. Five-card: discard your 6th card. Six-card: no discard; next player draws from stock or your discard. 3. **Round completion**: If caller is not the dealer, play continues so each player up to and including dealer gets one turn. 4. **Later calls**: Others may call if they equal or beat the best shown. 5. **Winner**: Highest combination wins the pot. Equal hands split the pot (or first-caller wins in some variants).',
    Player: '1. **Turn**: Draw one (stock or discard top), discard one. Hand stays at 5 cards until a call. 2. **Call**: With a winning combination after drawing, place it face up. Five-card: discard your 6th card. Six-card: no discard; next player draws from stock or your discard. 3. **Round completion**: If caller is not the dealer, play continues so each player up to and including dealer gets one turn. 4. **Later calls**: Others may call if they equal or beat the best shown. 5. **Winner**: Highest combination wins the pot. Equal hands split the pot (or first-caller wins in some variants).',
    objective: 'Form the highest five- or six-card combination and call to win the pot.',
    gameplay: '1. **Turn**: Draw one (stock or discard top), discard one. Hand stays at 5 cards until a call. 2. **Call**: With a winning combination after drawing, place it face up. Five-card: discard your 6th card. Six-card: no discard; next player draws from stock or your discard. 3. **Round completion**: If caller is not the dealer, play continues so each player up to and including dealer gets one turn. 4. **Later calls**: Others may call if they equal or beat the best shown. 5. **Winner**: Highest combination wins the pot. Equal hands split the pot (or first-caller wins in some variants).',
    keyRules: [
      'Turn-up card sets the wild rank for that deal.',
      'Winning combinations: 5 or 6 cards. No value for mixed-suit straights or non-sequence flushes.',
      "Paiute (Three Pairs) can only be called on a player's first draw (first round).",
      'If stock runs out, shuffle discard (except top) to form new stock.',
      'Pick from discard = must discard a different card; pick from stock = may discard the drawn card.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
